# Columns: any in-flow element goes inside a Columns (headings, lists, images, tables), and a Block with Keep together is not broken between columns.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Columns · Mixed content
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Heading 2
			Typography:
				Size: 11
				Line height: 14
				Bold: true
				Color: accent
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 4 0
		For element: List
			Box:
				Padding: 0 0 0 12
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
			Typography:
				Size: 9
				Line height: 12.5
		For style: box
			Box:
				Padding: 6
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
				Background: sand
			Typography:
				Size: 9
				Line height: 12.5
			Break:
				Keep together: true
	Section:
		Text: Columns
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Mixed content
		Paragraph: A `Columns` stacks any in-flow element as a `Block` does, and breaks it between columns with the rules of the page breaks. A `Block` with `Keep together: true` moves whole to the next column.
			Style: intro
		Columns:
			Column count: 3
			Gap: 14
			Heading 2:
				Text: The market
			Paragraph: The Saturday market returns to the main square with more stalls than ever.
			Image: examples/newsletter/market.jpg
				Alt: Stalls of the market in the main square
				Box:
					Width: 100%
					Margin: 0 0 6 0
			List:
				Marker: bullet
				List item:
					Text: Vegetables from the gardens
				List item:
					Text: Cheese from the hills
				List item:
					Text: Wood-fired bread
			Heading 2:
				Text: The walk
			Paragraph: The residents' association is organizing a walk along the river, from the old bridge at ten in the morning to the mill.
			Block:
				Style: box
				Text: Keep together: true. This block is not broken between two columns: it moves whole to the next one when it does not fit.
			Paragraph: Registration is open until Friday at the public library, and the walk is free for members.
